  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Avdheshkumar Shukarulal Pal And Anr vs State Of Maharashtra on 30 January, 2024 Author: N.J.Jamadar Bench: N.J.Jamadar 2024:Bhc-As:4668 907 ba In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No.398 Of 2024 Avdheshkumar Shukarulal Pal Avdesh Girijashankar Yadav ... Applican versus The State of Maharashtra ... Responde Mr. Amit Icham, for Applicants. Mrs. Geeta P. Mulekar, App for State. Mr. Vivek Vartak, Api Kalwa Police Station present. Coram: N.J.Jamadar, J. Date : 30 January 2024",
    "facts": "2. The applicants who are arraigned in C.R.No.637 of 2023 registe Kalwa Police Station for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 272, 27 read with 34 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 26(2)(i), 3(1)(zz)(iv), 5 30(2)(a), 27(3)(d), 27(3)(3) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, hav preferred this application to enlarge them on bail. 3. On 28 November 2023 the applicant No.1, who was at the wheel o truck being No.RJ-14/CH-1311 and the applicant No.2 who was as a cleaner the were found transporting Royal 1000 gutakha Dilbagh Plus Pan Masala and A Plu Chewing Tobacco in contravention of the provisions of the Food Safety and St Avdheshkumar Shukarulal Pal And Anr vs State Of Maharashtra on 30 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/120984678/ 1 Act, 2006. Police apprehended the applicants. Contraband articles were seize SSP 1/3 907 ba 398 of 202 4. Learned Counsel for the Applicants submitted that except the offence punishable under Section 328, all the offences are bailable. 6. Evidently, the contraband articles have been seized.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
